# 🎙️ Kavya – AI-Powered Voice Assistant

Kavya is a modern, browser-based voice assistant designed to provide an interactive, hands-free experience. Using the wake phrase **"Kavya"**, users can interact through voice commands or text input and receive spoken responses.

Built with React, TypeScript, Tailwind CSS, and browser speech technologies, Kavya offers a responsive interface, customizable voice settings, and quick commands for everyday tasks.

## ✨ Features

- 🎤 **Wake Phrase Detection:** Activate the assistant using "Kavya" while the webpage is open and active.
- 🗣️ **Speech Recognition:** Recognize voice commands using supported browser speech APIs.
- 🔊 **Text-to-Speech:** Hear responses through browser speech synthesis.
- 🌐 **Website Navigation:** Open Google, YouTube, Gmail, GitHub, LinkedIn, ChatGPT, and Lovable.
- ⏰ **Quick Commands:** Check the current time and date.
- 💬 **Conversation History:** View previous messages and assistant responses.
- 🌍 **Multilingual Settings:** Choose English (India), Telugu, or Hindi for speech output settings.
- ⚙️ **Customizable Voice:** Adjust speech rate, choose an available voice, and toggle spoken responses.
- ⌨️ **Text Input:** Interact with Kavya without using a microphone.
- 📱 **Responsive UI:** Designed for desktop and mobile screens.
- 🔐 **Privacy Awareness:** Includes microphone permission guidance and information about browser-based speech recognition.

## 🛠️ Tech Stack

| Technology | Purpose |
|---|---|
| React | User interface |
| TypeScript | Type-safe development |
| Tailwind CSS | Styling and responsive design |
| Web Speech API | Browser-based speech recognition |
| Speech Synthesis API | Spoken assistant responses |
| Vite | Development server and build tooling |

